WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.470
Welcome, and thank you for observing.

2
00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:08.580
In two minutes: what you do, and how your
phone helps.

3
00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:11.880
You watch and take notes.

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.160
You don't answer injects, and you don't
guide the team — even when they are stuck.

5
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.740
What you see becomes the evidence in the
report.

6
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:24.200
Your phone has three tabs.

7
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.617
Exercise shows what the room sees —

8
00:00:26.617 --> 00:00:31.540
plus what to watch for on this inject, and
which departments have answered.

9
00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.890
Never what they wrote.

10
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:40.740
To log a note: tap the type — Positive,
Needs improvement, or Critical gap.

11
00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.350
Check the department; it is filled in when
the inject names one.

12
00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:49.690
Write a few sentences and press "Log
note".

13
00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:53.720
A topic is optional — we classify
afterwards.

14
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.610
Prefer to speak?

15
00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:59.133
Tap the microphone, say your note,

16
00:00:59.133 --> 00:01:03.020
tap it again to stop, and correct the
words in the box.

17
00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:07.360
Speaking never sends anything — "Log note"
does.

18
00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:11.630
PlanProof keeps only the text, never the
recording.

19
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:17.160
Write what the team did, and what the plan
says — for example:

20
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.929
"The team called the supplier before
checking the contract;

21
00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:22.970
the plan says to check it first."

22
00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:25.790
Never name a person.

23
00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:31.340
A "Critical gap" note alerts the
facilitator at once.

24
00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:35.932
Use it when the plan itself fails or is
missing something critical —

25
00:01:35.932 --> 00:01:37.510
not for a slow decision.

26
00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:42.920
Messages reaches the facilitator: tap a
ready-made line —

27
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:48.820
"Our room needs more time", "A question
from our room" — and Send.

28
00:01:48.940 --> 00:01:52.200
Replies arrive at the top of your screen.

29
00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:58.412
After the exercise ends, your notes and
messages stay open for up to five hours —

30
00:01:58.412 --> 00:02:00.750
finish your notes while it's fresh.

31
00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:03.390
Then a one-minute survey.

32
00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:08.080
That's the only video on your phone today.

33
00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:11.010
Now set your phone to silent.

34
00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.740
Thank you.

